      "my_answer": "Dermatology (or primary care with dermatology referral if needed).",
      "rationale": "The problem is a common dermatologic issue; dermatologists are experts in skin‑related infections and shaving‑related folliculitis."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4",
      "question": "What are the key conditions to include in the differential diagnosis?",
      "my_answer": "Bacterial folliculitis, allergic contact dermatitis to shaving products, irritant dermatitis, hidradenitis suppurativa, viral warts (HPV), impetigo, scabies, and early cutaneous candidiasis.",
      "rationale": "All can present with papules/pustules on the thighs, but timing after shaving and follicular distribution point toward folliculitis while the others are considered for completeness."
